Fix: empty texture slots are no longer warned about on every draw

Applies to: rexglue-sdk nightly-20260921-923c1a59 (thirdparty/rexglue-sdk)
Apply with: git -C thirdparty/rexglue-sdk apply ../../patches/rexglue-sdk/0014-quiet-empty-texture-slots.patch
Status:     local patch (log noise; worth reporting upstream)

WHAT BROKE
  The log filled with
    Texture fetch constant (00024800 00000000 00000000 0AA80000 00000C03 00000018)
    has "invalid" type! ... --gpu_allow_invalid_fetch_constants=true.
  thousands of times per level load (9,665 warnings in the first 27 s of a
  save load, 6 distinct constants), a few per session otherwise. It buried
  real warnings and inflated the launcher's warning count.

WHY
  A texture fetch constant describes one sampler slot. Both kinds seen have
  type 0 ("invalid") AND base address 0 AND mip address 0: an empty slot,
  what D3D leaves after unbinding a texture (SetTexture(n, NULL)): one with
  only the sampler state set (filter / clamp in dword 0, swizzle in dword 3),
  one fully cleared. The game draws with such slots while a level's textures
  stream in. Nothing is bound for them either way: the warning's own advice
  (--gpu_allow_invalid_fetch_constants=true) lets the constant through, and
  the very next check ("base_page == 0 && mip_page == 0: no texture data at
  all") returns with nothing bound, exactly as now. The picture is unchanged.

FIX
  TextureCache::BindingInfoFromFetchConstant: an invalid-type constant with
  no base and no mip address returns quietly (same result as before). An
  invalid-type constant that DOES point at memory may matter: still warned,
  but once per distinct constant (up to 64), not per draw.

HOW FOUND
  Grouping the session log's warnings by message (6 distinct constants, all
  with dword 1 = 0 and dword 5's mip address = 0) and reading the texture
  cache's binding code.

diff --git a/src/graphics/pipeline/texture/cache.cpp b/src/graphics/pipeline/texture/cache.cpp
index 76f5600..bd9ccdf 100644
--- a/src/graphics/pipeline/texture/cache.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/pipeline/texture/cache.cpp
@@ -10,7 +10,10 @@
  */
 
 #include <algorithm>
+#include <array>
 #include <cstdint>
+#include <mutex>
+#include <set>
 #include <utility>
 
 #include <rex/assert.h>
@@ -910,17 +913,39 @@ void TextureCache::BindingInfoFromFetchConstant(const xenos::xe_gpu_texture_fetc
   switch (fetch.type) {
     case xenos::FetchConstantType::kTexture:
       break;
-    case xenos::FetchConstantType::kInvalidTexture:
+    case xenos::FetchConstantType::kInvalidTexture: {
       if (REXCVAR_GET(gpu_allow_invalid_fetch_constants)) {
         break;
       }
+      // An EMPTY slot: "invalid" type and no address at all is what D3D
+      // leaves after unbinding a texture (SetTexture(n, NULL)), and games
+      // draw with such slots (e.g. while textures stream in). Nothing is
+      // bound either way (with the flag above, the address check below would
+      // return just the same), so it isn't worth a warning: it was logged
+      // for every draw, thousands of lines per level load.
+      if (fetch.base_address == 0 && fetch.mip_address == 0) {
+        return;
+      }
+      // One that points at memory may matter: warned once per distinct
+      // constant (not per draw), up to 64 of them.
+      static std::mutex warned_mutex;
+      static std::set<std::array<uint32_t, 6>> warned;
+      {
+        std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(warned_mutex);
+        const std::array<uint32_t, 6> words = {fetch.dword_0, fetch.dword_1, fetch.dword_2,
+                                               fetch.dword_3, fetch.dword_4, fetch.dword_5};
+        if (warned.size() >= 64 || !warned.insert(words).second) {
+          return;
+        }
+      }
       REXGPU_WARN(
           "Texture fetch constant ({:08X} {:08X} {:08X} {:08X} {:08X} {:08X}) "
           "has \"invalid\" type! This is incorrect behavior, but you can try "
           "bypassing this by launching Xenia with "
-          "--gpu_allow_invalid_fetch_constants=true.",
+          "--gpu_allow_invalid_fetch_constants=true. (Logged once per constant.)",
           fetch.dword_0, fetch.dword_1, fetch.dword_2, fetch.dword_3, fetch.dword_4, fetch.dword_5);
       return;
+    }
     default:
       REXGPU_WARN(
           "Texture fetch constant ({:08X} {:08X} {:08X} {:08X} {:08X} {:08X}) "
